More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (661–670)
661. Improper Validation of Login Redirects
Open Redirect Vulnerability
Applications allow attackers to redirect users to malicious websites after login.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
662. Insecure Handling of Access Tokens
Access Token Exposure
Access tokens are stored or transmitted insecurely, allowing attackers to hijack accounts.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
663. Improper Validation of API Pagination Offsets
Pagination Offset Manipulation
Attackers manipulate pagination offsets to retrieve hidden records.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
664. Insecure Handling of Application Installation Packages
Installation Package Tampering
Application installation files can be modified to include malicious code.
💰 Typical payout: $700 – $12,000
665. Improper Validation of User Registration APIs
Registration Process Bypass
Attackers bypass registration restrictions such as invitation-only access.
